config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	bool "cadr-common"
	help
	  What every program on the processing system does before it
	  touches the fabric: the /dev/mem mapping, the EMIO tally's
	  marker-bit guard, and one prefixed log line at a time.  A
	  static library and its headers in the staging tree.

	  On the target it installs one file, /usr/share/cadr/fpgarc.sh:
	  the shell reader every init script hands the card's fpgarc to,
	  which gives each program the lines of the flags it owns and no
	  others.

	  Selected by the programs that use it rather than chosen on its
	  own.

# WHICH BOARD'S ADDRESS MAP THE PROGRAMS ARE BUILT WITH.  Every address a
# program maps --- the faces, the console, the machine's reserved memory and
# the tally the guard reads --- is a fact about the board, and
# src/cadr/cadr_board.h holds every board's.  The choice is made here, once,
# in the board's defconfig, and cadr-common carries it to every program: the
# library is compiled for it and the header it stages says which it is.  The
# Zynq-7000 boards are the default, so a defconfig that says nothing builds
# what it always built.
#
# The symbols are BR2_CADR_BOARD_* and not BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_*, because they
# are not packages: board/arty-z7-20/post-build.sh reads that namespace as
# the list of programs a defconfig asks for.
if BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
choice
	prompt "the board's address map"
	default BR2_CADR_BOARD_ZYNQ7000
	help
	  Which board the programs map the fabric of.

config BR2_CADR_BOARD_ZYNQ7000
	bool "Zynq-7000: the Arty Z7-20 and the Cora Z7-07S"

config BR2_CADR_BOARD_DE25_NANO
	bool "Agilex 5: the DE25-Nano"

endchoice
endif
